# Public host used to build handoff payload URLs (§4.9). No trailing slash.
# Until a host is chosen (§8 Q1), payload links are built from window.location
# at runtime and this is only a fallback for share text.
VITE_APP_HOST=https://vinrelay.example

# S4 only. The service-role key never appears here or anywhere in the client.
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# --- S4, in more detail ------------------------------------------------------
# The two names above are the only Supabase values the client reads. Get them from
# `supabase status` locally, or Settings -> API in the dashboard for a hosted
# project:
#   VITE_SUPABASE_URL        local: http://127.0.0.1:54321
#   VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY   local: the "anon key" line `supabase start` prints
# Put real values in `.env.local` (git-ignored via `*.local`). This file is
# committed and holds no key.
#
# There is deliberately no name here for the service-role key. It bypasses every
# RLS policy in supabase/migrations/0001_init.sql, it is needed only to delete an
# auth user, and the platform injects it into the delete-account Edge Function as
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY (CLAUDE.md rule 12). A `VITE_`-prefixed variable is
# compiled into the bundle, so a service-role key in one is a service-role key
# published to every visitor.
